    <briefdescription>
<para>How to write the tests. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>All the definitions are in the <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus" kindref="compound">micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus</ref></computeroutput> namespace, which the examples shorten with an alias:</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="preprocessor">#include<sp/>&lt;<ref refid="micro-test-plus_8h" kindref="compound">micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus.h</ref>&gt;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">namespace<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal">mt<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus" kindref="compound">micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus</ref>;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>The topics follow the structure of a test program:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>the runner, which starts and ends the session;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the suites, which group the test cases;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the test cases, which hold the checks;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the checks: the expectations, which are counted, and the requirements, which also stop the test case when they fail;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the conditions of the checks: the function comparators, the logical functions, and the exception checks;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the string utilities;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the customisation, for the application types and comparators;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the deprecated definitions, kept for the existing tests.  </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
